   **Standing constraint from the prior session, still in force (verbatim):** "entire garde les contextes de sessions dans une branche à part, n'y touche pas" — never delete, rename or otherwise touch git branches under the `entire/` prefix. Recorded at `C:\Users\anthoni\.claude\projects\C--Users-anthoni-projects-entire-anthnel-devdesk\memory\entire-branches-off-limits.md` with an index line in `MEMORY.md`.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Bubble Tea / Elm Architecture: router (`internal/app`) forwards keys to the active view; `Update()` is the only place model state may change (Rule 110)
   - `FormView` interface with `InEditMode() bool` — the predicate the router consults to decide whether it owns a key (`:`, `q`, `?`, and formerly `esc`)
   - lipgloss `MaxWidth()` truncates on rune boundaries without splitting ANSI escape sequences, unlike a plain slice or `theme.PadWithBg` (which pads short content but returns long content untouched)
   - Single-source-of-truth map pattern: `viewNames` drives parsing, alias resolution and tab-completion, with two invariant tests holding the ends together
   - "Inverted tests": tests written to assert broken behaviour and fail when the defect is fixed — turned around rather than deleted when the fix lands
   - Go 1.25 idioms: `maps.Copy`, `for i := range n`
   - Project rules referenced: Rule 111 (standard keybindings, `esc` = go back), Rule 122 (never let ANSI sequences be truncated), Rule 124 (footer/viewport layout), Rule 301/305 (golangci-lint + tests + build before commit)
   - Git: Entire mirror `origin` = `entire://aws-eu-central-1.entire.io/gh/anthnel/devdesk`; `main` is protected (PR-only); squash merges; `gh pr checks --watch`

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   - **`internal/app/app_header.go`** (D18 fix) — `buildShortcutLines` intended to clip the shortcut block to its column but padded instead. Changed:
     ```go
     		// Clip to the column. PadWithBg cannot do this — it pads a short line and
     		// returns a long one untouched — and a plain slice would cut an escape
     		// sequence in half, which is the hazard Rule 122 is about. MaxWidth
     		// truncates on rune boundaries and leaves the sequences intact.
     		if col2Width > 0 {
     			line = lipgloss.NewStyle().MaxWidth(col2Width).Render(line)
     		}
     		result[row] = line
     ```

   - **`internal/app/keys.go`** (D15 fix) — removed the `case "esc"` from `handleKeyMsg`'s switch and deleted `maybeQuitCommandMode` entirely. The replacement is a comment where the case used to be:
     ```go
     	// esc is deliberately absent: it belongs to the view. The router used to
     	// answer it whenever the view was not editing, which made esc-to-go-back dead
     	// code everywhere and forced views that wanted it to claim they were editing
     	// — a predicate about focused fields, overloaded into one about key
     	// ownership (§1.3 D15).
     	//
     	// Nothing is lost by handing it over: command mode is already closed by the
     	// time this switch runs (handleCommandMode answers first), so the router had
     	// nothing left to close.
     	default:
     		return a, a.forwardToActiveView(msg)
     ```

   - **`internal/command/parser.go`** (D16+D17 fix, fully rewritten) — now holds `viewNames`, `actionNames`, `actionAliases`, `normalize()`, a map-driven `ParseCommand`, a one-line `Parse`, a derived `GetAliases()` and a new `FullNames()`. `ViewNet` renamed to `ViewNetdiag` with value `"netdiag"`; `"net"`, `"gle"` and `"w"` are aliases. Key excerpts:
     ```go
     // viewNames maps every accepted spelling to the view it names. The key equal to
     // the ViewType is its full name; every other key is an alias.
     //
     // This map is the single source for both parsing and completion. They used to
     // be separate lists and had drifted: four views could be typed in full but not
